			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Migrate notification handlers to Batch 15-16 atoms\n\nConsolidate inline notification handler bodies in MountainVinegRPCService into delegations to atom functions in Vine::Server::Notification. Batch 15 migrates 8 handlers (ExtensionHostMessage, ExtensionActivated/ExtensionDeactivated, WebviewReady, ProgressStart/ProgressReport/ProgressEnd, LanguagesSetDocumentLanguage, WorkspaceApplyEdit, WindowShowTextDocument). Batch 16 adds 10 new handlers (WebviewLifecycle, WindowCreateTerminal, TerminalLifecycle covering 4 wire methods, DecorationTypeLifecycle, DebugLifecycle, StatusBarLifecycle covering 2 methods, StatusBarMessage, WindowShowMessage, RegisterCommand, UnregisterCommand).\n\nThis removes dead handler bodies at the bottom of match arms that were unreachable after Rust selected the first matching arm, keeping MountainVinegRPCService thin with one-line delegations. TerminalLifecycle and StatusBarLifecycle are group atoms covering methods sharing sky:// relay and provider-side drive.\n\nImpact: Consistent atom-layer dispatch pattern across all 26+ notification types.",
			"SHA": "07242d034472307f1b6610234b2c848d8def4c25"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T18:48:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Add notification atom handlers and stub disposition tracking\n\nCoordinate submodule updates across Mountain, Output, and Wind to complete VS Code notification IPC and improve stub diagnostics:\n\n- **Mountain:** Add 25 new notification atom handlers in Vine::Server::Notification covering output channel lifecycle (create, append, appendLine, clear, dispose, replace, show), status bar text updates, progress lifecycle, webview reverse messaging, provider unregistration, and misc handlers (openExternal, security.incident, set_language_configuration). Add ExtractDevTag module to parse Cocoon stdout [DEV:<TAG>] prefixes and re-emit under Mountain's matching tag for bootstrap-stage, ext-activate, config-prime, breaker filtering.\n\n- **Mountain Refactor:** Consolidate singular WindServiceHandler into plural WindServiceHandlers atoms - delete 24 dead duplicate files, re-implement 3 live handlers as atoms (extensions:install, extensions:uninstall, nativeHost.showOpenDialog). Add 9 new notification atoms: ExtensionActivated, ExtensionDeactivated, ExtensionHostMessage, LanguagesSetDocumentLanguage, ProgressStart, ProgressReport, ProgressEnd, WebviewReady, WorkspaceApplyEdit.\n\n- **Output:** Add __initialize stub for PlaywrightChannelClient constructor protocol version negotiation. Replace binary present=true/false stub-hit logging with three-state disposition: value (real payload), noop (intentionally undefined), drift (stub key missing - sync issue). Add explicit setExtensionGalleryManifest stub.\n\n- **Wind:** Add IPC stub for extensionGalleryManifest channel and __initialize to playwright stub. Enhance stub-hit logging with three-state disposition tracking using hasOwnProperty for reliable checking.\n\nImpact: Extension output channels, status bar, progress, and webview messaging now flow through Mountain. Cocoon bootstrap logs are tag-filterable. Stub drift detection helps developers distinguish sync issues from intentional undefined returns.",
			"SHA": "e7be1cbc0e4ef27e79a20cc9ada12db5165eecd3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T17:59:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Expand provider type coverage to full VS Code surface\n\nSubmodule sync to a3764731 coordinating Common and Mountain to add 7 new ProviderType enum variants: InlineEdit, MappedEdits, MultiDocumentHighlight, NotebookContent, RemoteAuthorityResolver, ResourceLabelFormatter, and ScmResourceGroup. This expands provider coverage from ~25 to 51 types.\n\nMountainVinegRPCService adds corresponding provider type handlers matching Cocoon's complete VS Code API shim, enabling extensions that register these previously-unhandled providers (e.g., GitLens, live share, remote tunnels) to activate successfully.\n\nRefs: b71ab93f22e526a1a9cc961706c66040fd2a9be6",
			"SHA": "c5fbb6ce3e814930df7b6d5ee79540c4a3c3a7fa"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T17:25:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Update Element submodule with Git IPC and tree-view round-trip\n\nSubmodule sync to 6f49be5 bringing coordinated changes across Common, Mountain, Output, Sky, and Wind:\n\n- **Git IPC:** Route localGit channel to Mountain's git subprocess handlers, fixing SourceControl panel hang with InvokeMountain(\"undefined:exec\"). Common adds Git IPC definitions (cancel, checkout, clone, exec, fetch, isAvailable, pull, revListCount, revParse).\n\n- **Tree-View:** Add tree:getChildren invoke handler in Mountain to forward to Cocoon's $provideTreeChildren. Sky adds cel:tree-view:create listener that re-dispatches as cel:tree-view:items, completing the F1.1 handoff contract.\n\n- **Diagnostics:** Add ext-scan and scheme-assets diagnostic tags. Add tauri-invoke timing instrumentation to distinguish webview transport latency from Mountain handler slowness.\n\nImpact: Built-in Git extension now functions with native git binaries. Extension tree views (GitLens, SCM, debug, tasks) render with data from providers.",
			"SHA": "a4feadcddd29b833207b91a5a20820f388483486"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T17:02:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Coordinate performance optimization and diagnostic instrumentation\n\nThree coordinated changes eliminate ~156 unnecessary Tauri IPC round-trips per editor boot and add comprehensive diagnostic capabilities:\n\n- **Performance (Wind/Output):** Add no-op IPC stubs for telemetryAppender (155 calls/boot) and mcpGalleryManifest (1 call/boot). These channels were falling through to Rust invoke with undefined handlers, adding latency to every editor startup. Stubs short-circuit in the TypeScript layer.\n\n- **Diagnostics (Mountain):** Add Git service handlers implementing the full localGit channel (clone, pull, checkout, revParse, fetch, etc.). Add SkyEmit instrumentation logging all Mountain→Wind/Sky emits under the sky-emit tag. Expand provider registration from 8 to 34+ types with scheme extraction.\n\n- **Diagnostics (Sky):** Track cel:* CustomEvent listener registration via document.addEventListener patching. Log consumer-present flag on every dispatch to identify orphan events (Mountain emits but no workbench listener). These are F1.1 indicators where features silently fail.\n\nImpact: Editor startup latency reduced by eliminating ~156 IPC round-trips. Developers can now audit SkyEmit traffic via LAND_DEV_LOG=sky-emit and identify dead event routes via cel-dispatch consumer-present=false.",
			"SHA": "2d95bc0ae30754abf7c20dabc8b7feb319499429"
		}
	],
